  "oracle": {
    "kind": "python_callable",
    "module": "oracle_entry",
    "callable": "evaluate",
    "sys_path": "exploration/stellarator_e2e/studies",
    "note": "Package-owned oracle seam. evaluate(point) takes a mapping of qualified entry keys to floats and returns a mapping of qualified channel names to floats; it wraps the independent pure-Python oracle verify_stellaris.py, whose current live radius operands follow model-owned plant R. ANNEX.md section Current oracle comparison coverage lists the seventeen native channels outside its 141-channel map. The module also publishes a fixed-name companion, operand_bindings() -> {constraint_id: {source_name: {kind, key}}}, which says which qualified input key or channel each predicate operand means. A generic verifier requires both and fails closed on anything unresolved: on this package one operand of five constraints resolves to nothing by name at all, so a tool that inferred bindings would compare the wrong number and read as a pass."
  }
